[s0l0!-header][h1]Nested if else Statements[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

C++ provides the option of nesting an unlimited number of if/else statements.
[s0l0!-header][b]For example:[/b][/s0l0!-header] [code format="cpp" codeId="198"]int age = 18;
if (age > 14) {
  if(age >= 18) {
    cout << "Adult";
  }
  else {
    cout << "Teenager";
  }
}
else {
  if (age > 0) {
    cout << "Child";
  }
  else {
    cout << "Something's wrong";
  }
}[/code]
[note]Remember that all [b]else [/b]statements must have corresponding [b]if[/b] statements.[/note]

